<h1><table><tr><td>PS! Game Corner Shiny Pokedex</td></tr></table></h1>
<h3><span style="letter-spacing:5px;"><table><tr>
<td><a style="text-decoration:none; color: silver" href="https://htmlpreview.github.io/?https://github.com/bouquets-ps/gc-pokedex/blob/main/about">ABOUT</a></td>
<td style="width: 50px"></td><td><a style="text-decoration:none; color: silver" href="https://htmlpreview.github.io/?https://github.com/bouquets-ps/gc-pokedex/blob/main/pokedex">POKEDEX</a></td>
<td style="width: 50px"></td><td>FAQ</td>
</tr></table></span></h3>
</center>

<hr><br>

<b><span style="display: inline-block ; height: 30px ; width: 40px ; background: transparent url(&quot;https://play.pokemonshowdown.com/sprites/pokemonicons-sheet.png?v16&quot;) no-repeat scroll -360px -2580px"></span>When I play a shiny Pokemon card, does the Pokedex get updated automatically?</b>
<br><br>No. Updates are done manually by <b><font color="#2884c6">bouquets</font></b> when she:
<li>spots a new shiny Pokemon displayed in the room.
<li>reviews user submissions.

<br><br><b><span style="display: inline-block ; height: 30px ; width: 40px ; background: transparent url(&quot;https://play.pokemonshowdown.com/sprites/pokemonicons-sheet.png?v16&quot;) no-repeat scroll -360px -2580px"></span>How can I help updating the Pokedex?</b>
<br><br>Fill in <a style="text-decoration:none; color: silver" href="https://forms.gle/KLdyS6DxU5jXL7wq9">the Pokemon submission form</a>. You are free to submit yours and other users' shiny Pokemon.

<br><br><b><span style="display: inline-block ; height: 30px ; width: 40px ; background: transparent url(&quot;https://play.pokemonshowdown.com/sprites/pokemonicons-sheet.png?v16&quot;) no-repeat scroll -360px -2580px"></span>Does the Pokedex register all Pokemon, including forms?</b>
<br><br>The Pokedex registers all Pokemon with a positive dex number, excluding forms.

<br><br><b><span style="display: inline-block ; height: 30px ; width: 40px ; background: transparent url(&quot;https://play.pokemonshowdown.com/sprites/pokemonicons-sheet.png?v16&quot;) no-repeat scroll -360px -2580px"></span>What are the games where shiny Pokemon cards can be played?</b>
<br><br><table border="2" cellpadding="5">
<tr><td style="width: 250px"><b>Game</b><td><b>Unavailable Pokemon</b></td></tr>
<tr><td>Axew's Battle Cards</td><td rowspan="2"></td></tr>
<tr><td>Shuckle's Defense Cards</td></tr>
<tr><td>Stakataka's Card Tower</td><td>Manaphy, Pachirisu, Phione</td></tr>
<tr><td>Bulbasaur's Uno</td><td>Doduo, Greninja, Kecleon, Inkay, Machamp, Magnemite, Slaking, Spinda</td></tr>
<tr><td>Blissey's Egg Cards</td><td>Chansey, Ditto, Happiny, Undiscovered Pokemon, Water 2 Pokemon, Water 3 Pokemon</td></tr>
</table>
<br>In addition, Pokemon with no GIFs on PS! are unavailable in all games.

<br><br><b><span style="display: inline-block ; height: 30px ; width: 40px ; background: transparent url(&quot;https://play.pokemonshowdown.com/sprites/pokemonicons-sheet.png?v16&quot;) no-repeat scroll -360px -2580px"></span>Can I use the action card Transform to hunt for specific Pokemon?</b>
<br><br>Yes! Using Transform is perfectly fine.

<br><br><b><span style="display: inline-block ; height: 30px ; width: 40px ; background: transparent url(&quot;https://play.pokemonshowdown.com/sprites/pokemonicons-sheet.png?v16&quot;) no-repeat scroll -360px -2580px"></span>Can I hunt for shiny Pokemon in Game Workshop?</b>
<br><br>No. Every screenshot submission must contain Lady Monita's message about the Luck of the Draw achievement, and Game Workshop does not have achievements enabled.

